# The build context is the repository root, and everything in it is left out except the paths
# the Dockerfile copies, so local data, environments, caches and development files never reach a
# build. A path the Dockerfile copies must be let in here, or the build stops at that COPY.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY.md
!src/
!app/pyproject.toml
!app/uv.lock
!app/demo/
!app/scripts/fetch_demos.py
!app/scripts/list_licenses.py
!app/server/
!app/web/

# Inside what is let in: the page's offline fixtures and the tools that build them are for
# development only, so the image never serves them. Tests, caches and data files stay out too.
# The PBMC FCS files are fetched and sha256-checked by the build, so local copies stay out.
app/web/fixtures
app/web/tools
**/tests
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/*.fcs
**/*.npz
app/demo/data/*.part
